{"author":{"id":"1d5f412cdeafe9987ad9876b0995bf5032718543d34c038a50cdb41808e9874c"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1788305123,"nonce":"FI3rONt2pZ3vAZR7wsCccfo5ClY=","metadata":{"github-id":"I_kwDOULVc1M8AAAABPPhdkg","github-url":"https://github.com/kanya-approve/torram-ng/issues/6","origin":"github"},"title":"remove_hard_links keys on st_ino without st_dev, breaking multi-drive scans","message":"```python\ndef remove_hard_links(files):\n    inode_to_filename = {}\n    for filename in files:\n        stat_info = os.stat(filename)\n        inode_to_filename[stat_info[stat.ST_INO]] = filename\n    return inode_to_filename.values()\n```\n\nInode numbers are only unique within a filesystem. Two genuinely different files on two different drives routinely share an inode number, and this dict silently discards one of them.\n\nThat directly defeats the tool's main use case — scanning several disks for copies of the same torrent. The candidate that gets dropped may be the one holding the only good copy of some pieces.\n\nThe key must be `(st_dev, st_ino)`.","files":null}]}